Physiological carryover
The mind and body do not reset together.
After fear, exertion, embarrassment, pain, or stress, preserve:
elevated pulse;
altered breathing;
residual trembling;
dry mouth;
nausea;
sweating;
muscle fatigue;
tenderness;
