Treat environments as persistent participants.
Rooms and objects retain the consequences of earlier actions:
damp towels remain damp;
food cools;
condensation dries;
chairs remain displaced;
opened drawers remain open unless closed;
smells linger and mix;
footprints or water marks remain;
devices continue humming;
